---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import InfoPage from "@components/InfoPage.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About NepalRanks, community-driven rankings of Nepal"
  description="NepalRanks is a community-driven platform where the public decides Nepal's rankings through upvotes and downvotes. Read about the mission, the independence model and the build roadmap."
>
  <InfoPage eyebrow="About">
    <h1>About NepalRanks</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>NepalRanks is a community ranking platform for Nepal</strong> built on one
      simple conviction: rankings of things people use every day, banks, internet
      providers, universities, cities, restaurants, should be decided by the people who
      use them, not by an editorial desk or the highest bidder.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>
      The community votes on named rankings such as <em>Best Banks in Nepal</em> or
      <em>Best Momo Spots in Kathmandu</em>. Every entry carries an upvote score, a
      downvote score and a net score, and <strong>the net score alone determines the
      position</strong>. Discussion travels with each entry, so voters can always see
      <em>why</em> something sits where it sits.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not sell positions, boost rankings or accept payment for placement.</li>
      <li>Administrators create categories and keep discussions civil, they cannot move an entry.</li>
      <li>There is no editorial ranking. If a position looks wrong, the fix is more voters, not a press release.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where the project stands</h2>
    <p>
      NepalRanks is a live platform: every vote is counted the second it is cast, every
      comment appears instantly, and page order moves with the scores. Rankings are seeded
      by the team and grow with the community, city by city. <strong>Google sign-in</strong> guards voting and commenting, your nickname is public, your email stays between you and the moderation team, and
      community-submitted rankings are next.
    </p>

    <h2>The name and the promise</h2>
    <p>
      Our tagline is <strong>Your Voice. Your Rankings.</strong> The platform exists to
      make that promise mechanically true: your vote counts exactly as much as anyone
      else's, and every ranking movement is visible in the numbers.
    </p>
  </InfoPage>
</BaseLayout>
